/F1 12 Tf
72 760 Td
(Fractal Explorer - simple explanation) Tj
T*
(1) This repo is a small web app that lets you explore fractals in your browser.) Tj
T*
(   The Rust server generates image tiles; the HTML page lets you pan and zoom.) Tj
T*
T*
(2) Right-clicking the Mandelbrot view jumps to a Julia set.) Tj
T*
(   The clicked point becomes the Julia constant c, and the page refreshes.) Tj
T*
T*
(3) The Detail slider controls how many times each point is checked.) Tj
T*
(   Higher detail = slower but sharper deep zooms; lower detail = faster but less precise.) Tj
T*
T*
(4) The server logic in src/main.rs works like this:) Tj
T*
(   - read the tile request from the browser) Tj
T*
(   - map each pixel to a point in the complex plane) Tj
T*
(   - repeatedly apply the fractal formula to see whether the point escapes) Tj
T*
(   - choose a color based on how quickly it escapes) Tj
T*
(   - package the 256x256 result as a PNG and send it back) Tj
T*
T*
(5) The browser page in static/index.html provides the controls.) Tj
T*
(   It uses Leaflet for map-like navigation and keeps the current view in the URL.) Tj
ET
endstream
